{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "JHN",
  "chapter": 4,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When therefore the Lord knew that the Pharisees had heard that Jesus made and baptized more disciples than John,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(Though Jesus himself baptized not, but his disciples,)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He left Judea, and departed again into Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he must needs go through Samaria.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he cometh to a city of Samaria, which is called Sychar, near to the parcel of ground, that Jacob gave to his son Joseph.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now Jacob's well was there. Jesus therefore being wearied with ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " journey, sat thus on the well: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " it was about the sixth hour.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "There cometh a woman of Samaria to draw water: Jesus saith to her, Give me to drink.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "(For his disciples had gone to the city to buy provisions.)",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then saith the woman of Samaria to him, How is it that thou, being a Jew, askest drink of me, who am a woman of Samaria? for the Jews have no dealings with the Samaritans.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered and said to her, If thou knewest the gift of God, and who it is that saith to thee, Give me to drink; thou wouldst have asked him, and he would have given thee living water.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman saith to him, Sir, thou hast nothing to draw with, and the well is deep: from whence then hast thou that living water?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Art thou greater than our father Jacob, who gave us the well, and drank of it himself, and his children, and his cattle?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus answered and said to her, Whoever drinketh of this water, shall thirst again:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But whoever drinketh of the water that I shall give him, shall never thirst; but the water that I shall give him, shall be in him a well of water springing up into everlasting life.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman saith to him, Sir, give me this water, that I may not thirst, neither come hither to draw.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to her, Go, call thy husband, and come hither.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman answered and said, I have no husband. Jesus said to her, Thou hast well said, I have no husband:",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For thou hast had five husbands, and he whom thou now hast, is not thy husband: in that thou hast spoken truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman saith to him, Sir, I perceive that thou art a prophet.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our fathers worshiped in this mountain; and ye say, that in Jerusalem is the place where men ought to worship.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to her, Woman, believe me, the hour cometh, when ye shall neither in this mountain, nor yet at Jerusalem, worship the Father.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Ye worship ye know not what: we know what we worship, for salvation is from the Jews.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the hour cometh, and now is, when the true worshipers shall worship the Father in spirit and in truth: for the Father seeketh such to worship him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "God ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a Spirit: and they that worship him, must worship ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in spirit and in truth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman saith to him, I know that Messiah cometh, who is called Christ; when he is come, he will tell us all things.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to her, I that speak to thee am ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "he",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And upon this came his disciples, and marveled that he talked with the woman: yet no man said, What seekest thou? or, Why talkest thou with her?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.28",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.28",
      "verse": 28,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The woman then left her waterpot, and went into the city, and saith to the men,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.29",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.29",
      "verse": 29,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Come, see a man who hath told me all things that ever I did: is not this the Christ?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.30",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.30",
      "verse": 30,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then they went out of the city, and came to him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.31",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.31",
      "verse": 31,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the mean while his disciples prayed him, saying, Master, eat.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.32",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.32",
      "verse": 32,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But he said to them, I have food to eat that ye know not of.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.33",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.33",
      "verse": 33,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore said the disciples one to another, Hath any man brought him ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "aught",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to eat?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.34",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.34",
      "verse": 34,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to them, My food is to do the will of him that sent me, and to finish his work.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.35",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.35",
      "verse": 35,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Say not ye, There are yet four months, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "then",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cometh harvest? behold, I say to you, Lift up your eyes, and look on the fields; for they are white already to harvest.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.36",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.36",
      "verse": 36,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he that reapeth receiveth wages, and gathereth fruit to life eternal: that both he that soweth, and he that reapeth, may rejoice together.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.37",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.37",
      "verse": 37,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And herein is that saying true, One soweth, and another reapeth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.38",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.38",
      "verse": 38,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I sent you to reap that on which ye bestowed no labor: other men labored, and ye have entered into their labors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.39",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.39",
      "verse": 39,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And many of the Samaritans of that city believed on him for the saying of the woman, who testified, He told me all that ever I did.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.40",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.40",
      "verse": 40,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So when the Samaritans had come to him, they besought him that he would tarry with them: and he abode there two days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.41",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.41",
      "verse": 41,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And many more believed, because of his own word;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.42",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.42",
      "verse": 42,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And said to the woman, Now we believe, not because of thy saying: for we have heard ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ourselves, and know that this is indeed the Christ, the Savior of the world.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.43",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.43",
      "verse": 43,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now after two days he departed thence, and went into Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.44",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.44",
      "verse": 44,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For Jesus himself testified that a prophet hath no honor in his own country.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.45",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.45",
      "verse": 45,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then when he had come into Galilee, the Galileans received him, having seen all the things that he did at Jerusalem at the feast: for they also went to the feast.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.46",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.46",
      "verse": 46,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So Jesus came again into Cana of Galilee, where he made the water wine. And there was a certain nobleman, whose son was sick at Capernaum.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.47",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.47",
      "verse": 47,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When he heard that Jesus had come from Judea into Galilee, he went to him, and besought him that he would come down, and heal his son: for he was at the point of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.48",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.48",
      "verse": 48,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then said Jesus to him, Except ye see signs and wonders, ye will not believe.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.49",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.49",
      "verse": 49,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The nobleman saith to him, Sir, come down ere my child dieth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.50",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.50",
      "verse": 50,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Jesus saith to him, Go; thy son liveth. And the man believed the word that Jesus had spoken to him, and he departed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.51",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.51",
      "verse": 51,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as he was now going down, his servants met him, and told ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", saying, Thy son liveth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.52",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.52",
      "verse": 52,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he inquired of them the hour when he began to amend: and they said to him, Yesterday at the seventh hour the fever left him.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.53",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.53",
      "verse": 53,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So the father knew that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at the same hour in which Jesus said to him, Thy son liveth: and he himself believed, and his whole house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "JHN.4.54",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:JHN.4.54",
      "verse": 54,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " again the second miracle ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Jesus performed, when he had come from Judea into Galilee.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
